gguf-rco step 6h (0036): the IQ3_S decode on a tile-major repack with 16-byte
copies. After loading, every IQ3_S shard (or single-type weight) is repacked
once into tiles of 64 rows x 112 bytes per (64-row tile, k-block), the fields
word-aligned, and the decode calls of that tensor go through a custom op onto
the tile kernel; the raw rows stay for the prefill's dequantiser (a measurement
build: the IQ3_S bytes are held twice). Applies after 0022-0029.

